+# Validation report — v0.2.5
+
+Fresh compilation on Linux with rustc 1.99.1 and the included Cargo.lock. The binary
+was driven through a real POSIX pseudo-terminal with keyboard input, a separate TLS
+server, disposable accounts and SQLite databases. No prebuilt executable is shipped.
+
+| Check | Evidence |
+| --- | --- |
+| Rust tests | `tests/latest-rust-run.txt` |
+| Fresh build | `tests/latest-build-run.txt` |
+| Clippy, all targets, warnings denied | `tests/latest-clippy-run.txt` |
+| Formatting | `tests/latest-format-run.txt` |
+| Real CLI/TUI journey | `tests/latest-terminal-run.txt` |
+
+## Reproduce
+
+From the project root, configure `.env` as described in README, then:
+
+```sh
+cargo fmt --check
+cargo clippy --locked --all-targets -- -D warnings
+cargo test --locked
+cargo build --locked
+python3 tests/terminal_smoke.py
+```
+
+The terminal test sets its own synthetic configuration. For a custom Cargo target
+folder, set `VOTING_TEST_BINARY` to the absolute compiled binary path. It needs Python
+3 and POSIX PTYs; there are no extra Python dependencies. It waits for visible backend
+responses rather than assuming registration is rendered when its transaction commits.
+
+## Actual terminal journey
+
+1. Reject empty signup, use engineer OTP, create admin and district-official accounts.
+2. Generate TLS identities and start a separate server. Connect a client without the pepper.
+3. Log in as admin, create an election, edit positions/candidates, reopen saved configuration.
+4. Reject empty, underage and unknown-ID registrations; register a valid voter.
+5. Verify the PIN is in the phone-named inbox and absent from terminal output. Confirm receipt.
+6. Reject duplicate registration and open Admin → View Audit Log.
+7. Reject voting before opening; open as DO. Reject an incomplete ballot, then submit.
+8. Check one choice per position, private thank-you receipt, logout, and repeat-vote rejection.
+9. Close, tally and announce. Verify the winner screen says `Winner: Red Burger`.
+10. Return from results to lifecycle controls. Attempt two more tallies and another announcement.
+    Require NEW warning records and unchanged totals/timestamps; exactly one successful tally.
+11. Inspect JSON traces and SQLite audit/security records: lifecycle and rejection events exist;
+    voter identity, phone, PIN, candidate selections and voter actor IDs do not appear in traces.
+
+## Audit coverage
+
+| Scenario | Recording/check |
+| --- | --- |
+| Staff signup/login and OTP | Provision/setup/login events; failed password/OTP, expiry, lock and blocked attempts; role/challenge replay tests |
+| Election/position/candidate changes | Staff actor and election attribution; CRUD tests; real terminal candidate editing; audit failure rolls back the edit |
+| Registration | Unknown ID, SQL-shaped ID, name/DOB/phone mismatch, submitted/canonical minor DOB and unavailable registry: warning with no applicant identity; no credentials/enrollment created |
+| PIN receipt | Yes: severity 0; no: severity 2; no subject voter ID; invalid owner/target rejected |
+| Lifecycle | Open/close/tally/announce; repeat tally/announcement warning count and timestamp immutability; failed tally audit rolls back totals |
+| Voter failures | Daily category counters only, including unauthenticated PIN failure, OTP failure/expiry, blocked/locked attempts, authorization/request/timeout and client errors |
+| Client error injection | Arbitrary screen/message text is discarded; staff receives fixed-message audit; voter gets anonymous counter, no error-report row |
+| Role/ownership misuse | Direct endpoint attempts with wrong roles and cross-admin ownership rejected; API checks independent of UI |
+| Incident flag | Owning admin sees severity 2; wrong role/owner denied; cancelled elections remain available in audit selection |
+| Log tampering/privacy | SQL triggers reject audit/security UPDATE/DELETE and voter-identifying inserts; no individual successful-vote audit |
+| TLS/framing/deadlines | Untrusted CA/hostname/client cert, plaintext and bad frames rejected; transport aggregates and timeouts; stalled connection closes |
+| Notification failure | Committed audit survives email delivery failure; outbox retries; no secret or ballot content in notifications |
+
+See STRIDE.md for attack categories and test names in the transcripts. Security tests
+use isolated local targets only. Tests use low bcrypt cost in Rust fixtures; the real
+TUI run uses the normal application cost. Timeouts deliberately take about 11 seconds.
+
+## Boundaries
+
+This is functional and adversarial regression testing, not a production penetration
+test, certification or proof that every vulnerability is absent. Native Windows/macOS
+runs were unavailable; accepted-socket blocking mode has a portable regression test.
+The registry, SMS and email delivery are classroom simulations. Same-host file owners
+can read inboxes and replace databases/drop triggers. Existing historical audit rows
+are preserved, not scrubbed. JSON tracing is asynchronous; SQLite is authoritative.
